subject: fix(rate-limiter): exempt RSC prefetches from middleware-layer limiter

The middleware rate limiter (checkRateLimit in dashboardGuard.js, wired via

src/proxy.js) was counting Next-internal ?_rsc= navigations and /_next/* asset

requests against the same per-IP bucket as ordinary navigation, so a burst of

RSC prefetches from a heavy dashboard page could 429 the very navigation that

triggered them — the middleware-layer twin of the TCP-layer Finding #8/#14 bug.

- Added isNextInternalRequest() exempting /_next/* paths and any request carrying

  a _rsc query param, mirroring isNextInternal in custom-server.rate-limiter.js.

- Defensive ?. on searchParams to tolerate test fakes.

- fakeRequest test helper gained a search parameter for query strings.

- 3 regression tests (RSC exempt, /_next/ exempt, ordinary still limited).

- 24/24 middleware tests pass.

Resolves Finding #16.

